rket Mills began as the Lowell Manufacturing Company complex, and its Brussels Weave Mill is the oldest surviving building in that complex.","source_url":"https://home.nps.gov/lowe/planyourvisit/redevelopment-rove.htm","source_title":"Lowell Waterways Redevelopment Rove — Lowell National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The walking route begins at Market Mills, 246 Market Street.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mack-plaza","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Mack Plaza","title":"Pick up the Waterpower Walk","subtitle":"Market Street and Shattuck Street corridor","notes":"Use Mack Plaza as the handoff from Market Street to the Waterpower Walk, then follow the route to notice how the canals shaped downtown.","short_summary":"A documented starting point for the park’s Waterpower Walk.","evidence_claim":"The park directs visitors to pick up the Waterpower Walk at Mack Plaza, at the corner of Shattuck and Market streets.","source_url":"https://home.nps.gov/lowe/planyourvisit/redevelopment-rove-part-2.htm","source_title":"Redevelopment Rove Part 2 — Lowell National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"At the corner of Shattuck and Market streets, across from the Visitor Center.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"patrick-j-mogan-cultural-center","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Patrick J. Mogan Cultural Center","title":"Compare two exhibits about Lowellians","subtitle":"French Street corridor — 40 French Street","notes":"Enter from French Street and move through the boarding-house and One City, Many Cultures exhibits to connect industrial and community histories.","short_summary":"A free exhibit center with two perspectives