reated working 1920s-era weave room.","evidence_claim":"The museum includes a recreated 1920s-era weave room with operating power looms, artifacts, interactive exhibits, and videos.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/lowe/planyourvisit/boott-cotton-mills-museum.htm","source_title":"Boott Cotton Mills Museum — Lowell National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"At 115 John Street; museum admission is ticketed and operating hours are seasonal.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"suffolk-mill-turbine-exhibit","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Suffolk Mill Turbine Exhibit","title":"Trace waterpower to a still-operating turbine","subtitle":"Suffolk Street corridor — 660 Suffolk Street","notes":"Book or join the guided option when available, then look for how the Northern Canal sits beside the turbine exhibit’s historic machinery.","short_summary":"A guided-tour site centered on a nineteenth-century water turbine.","evidence_claim":"The exhibit’s still-operating turbine dates to 1853 and demonstrates how nineteenth-century Lowell mills generated power.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/lowe/planyourvisit/placestogo.htm","source_title":"Places To Go — Lowell National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"At 660 Suffolk Street alongside the Northern Canal; accessible by guided tour only.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"kerouac-park","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Jack Kerouac Commemorative","title":"Read Kerouac excerpts in the memorial plaza","subtitle":"Bridge Street corridor — Kerouac Park","notes":"Walk the commemorative path in Kerouac Park and read the installed excerpts, using the circles and cross as part of the artist’s intended design.","short_summary":"A memorial plaza dedicated to Lowell-born writer Jack Kerouac.","evidence_claim":"The Jack Kerouac Commemorative in Kerouac Park contains excerpts from Kerouac’s writing and was dedicated in 1988.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/lowe/learn/historyculture/jackkerouac.htm","source_title":"Jack Kerouac — Lowell National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located in Kerouac Park on Bridge Street.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ayer-lofts","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Ayer Lofts","title":"Spot the former medicine laboratory building","subtitle":"Market Street corridor — entry/gallery on Middle Street","notes":"View the restored Ayer building from Market Street, then use the park’s account to identify its earlier laboratory role and later artist-loft conversion.","short_summary":"A restored former laboratory building with a documented adaptive reuse.","evidence_claim":"The J. C. Ayer Company used the building for manufacturing laboratories until 1917; it reopened as artist work-and-live lofts in 2000.","source_url":"https://home.nps.gov/lowe/planyourvisit/redevelopment-rove-part-2.htm","source_title":"Redevelopment Rove Part 2 — Lowell National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"On Market Street; the source notes first-floor gallery entry on Middle Street.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"father-johns-medicine-building","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Father John’s Medicine Building","title":"Find the painted patent-medicine sign","subtitle":"Palmer Street corridor — near Market Street","notes":"Walk one block down Palmer Street from Market Street and look up 